<p>In a multi-user environment, a thin client environment, or a "Point 
 and Print" environment, users can share the one click presets registered 
 by the Administrator.</p>
<p class="Note">Note:</p>
<ul>
<li><p>To make this setting, you must be logged in as 
 an Administrator.</p></li>
</ul>
<ol>
<li><p>In the <span class="Term-OS">Devices and Printers</span> 
 window, open the printer properties dialog box.</p></li>
</ol>
<ol start="2">
<li><p>Click the <span class="Term-Soft">Advanced Options</span> 
 tab.</p></li>
<li><p>Click <span class="Term-Soft">Manage...</span>, 
 and the <span class="Term-Soft">Manage One Click Preset List</span> dialog 
 box appears.</p></li>
<li><p>Select the one click preset name which you want 
 to share, and then select the <span class="Term-Soft">Share</span> check 
 box.</p></li>
<li><p>If necessary, click <span class="Term-Soft">Up</span> 
 or <span class="Term-Soft">Down</span> to change the display order of the 
 one click presets.</p></li>
<li><p>If necessary, change the one click preset name 
 and comment in the boxes below.</p></li>
</ol>
<div class="help-step-extra">
<ul>
<li><p class="Normal-indent">The name can 
 be up to 128 single-byte or 64 double-byte characters.</p></li>
<li><p class="Normal-indent">The comment 
 can be up to 512 single-byte or 256 double-byte characters. You can insert 
 line breaks.</p></li>
</ul>
</div>
<ol start="7">
<li><p>Make sure the settings have been changed in the 
 list. If everything is correct, click <span class="Term-OS">OK</span> to 
 save the changes and close the <span class="Term-Soft">Manage One Click 
 Preset List</span> dialog box.</p></li>
<li><p>Click <span class="Term-OS">OK</span>.<br/>
 The printer properties dialog box closes.</p></li>
</ol>
